   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1 Number of provincial electoral and civil registration offices with recruited and trained staff, sufficient physical and technical infrastructure to accommodate their mandate;
1.2 Number of new increased and trained permanent staff at HQs and provincial offices, including joint training activities with the CRVS Department;
1.3 Number of formalised EC internal regulations and VEO operational procedures drafted and endorsed.
1.4 The percentage of progress in codifying and digitizing institutional memory of EC/VEO systems and procedures, including congregating files to the Government Document Management System (Saperion);
1.5 No of electoral administrative processes where gender is mainstreamed, and gender disaggregated
2.1 Proportion of eligible voters who are registered to vote, disaggregated by sex, age, and location &#x2013; to be done on a yearly basis
2.2 Number of voters issued with national ID card disaggregated by gender (replacing the electoral cards)
2.3 Percentage of merge of databases/transition to new voter registration model.
2.4 Expected number of duplicated and deceased citizens removed from the Civil and Voter registries.
2.5 New components developed and updated for Civil and Voter registration systems. 
3.1 Number of new partnerships with civil society developed (Women, PWDs, churches), as well as regional bodies, and national and international stakeholders.
3.2 Percentage of matrix on gender tracking in elections developed, including gender-disaggregated data on all aspects of the electoral administration - done on an annual basis.
3.3 Percentage of matrix on gender tracking in Civil registry developed, including gender-disaggregated data &#x2013; done on annual basis.
3.4 Assessment on civic understanding and access to information implemented.
4.1 Number of viable and practical reform proposals developed
4.2 Number of electoral staff (gender disaggregated) trained on new reform measures 
4.3 Number of key stakeholders trained on new reform measures</narrative>
    </description>
